Module mere "The Moonglass Mere" {
  Description "A reed-bed at the edge of a mere, and a sluice-house where hounds lair: an adventure with its own kinds of things and creatures, which another adventure may name the same and mean otherwise.".
  Place shore "the shore of the mere" is wilderness.
  Place reeds "the reed-bed" is room within shore at 0, 0.
  Place sluice "the sluice-house" is room within shore at 1, 0.
  Passage causeway "the causeway" is causeway between reeds and sluice taking 5 minutes.
  Company party "You" of 1 at reeds.
  // What this water makes that nowhere else does: glass of moonlight, worth something to whoever buys glass.
  Kind moonglass "a shard of moonglass" is treasure worth 50 weighing 0 described "Glass the mere makes of moonlight on still nights; it holds a little of the light it was made of.".
  // The hounds of these reed-beds, of the wolf's kind and as quick to hold their ground.
  Species mere_hound "a mere hound" like wolf temperament territorial described "A long grey hound of the reed-beds that hunts along the water's edge.".
  Item shard "a shard of moonglass" is moonglass at reeds.
  Person hounds "the mere hounds" at sluice { Role "the hounds of the sluice". Species mere_hound. Numbers 2. Level 1. Lair sluice. }
  // The sluice that lets the mere down, worked from the house.
  Thing gate "the sluice gate" at sluice {
    State shut "The sluice gate is down, and the mere stands high against it.".
    State open "The sluice gate is wound up, and the mere runs out under it, talking.".
    Change wind "Wind the sluice gate up" from shut to open.
  }
  Person ness "Ness" at reeds { Role "a reed-cutter". Ancestry human. Calling commoner. Peaceable. }
  Topic ness_glass with ness "Ask {ness} about the moonglass" when true once {
    Says "'The mere makes it on still nights,' says {ness}. 'It keeps a little of the moon in it. The glass-buyers at the works pay for it, when they come.'".
  }
  Observe reeds_scene at reeds when true "Reeds taller than you on every side, and the mere beyond them, flat and grey.".
  Observe sluice_scene at sluice when true "A house of black timber over the sluice, smelling of hounds.".
  Goal false.
}
